    "narrative": "Our offensive outlook for May 30th hinges on exploiting the soft matchup against Feltner, who anchors a significant portion of our starting nine. **Matt Chapman** (70.06) and **Daulton Varsho** (69.94) represent our most efficient plays today. **Matt Chapman** benefits from the favorable park factor and Feltner\u2019s slow delivery, which provides a high-probability environment for stolen bases, a critical necessity for our 5x5 build. Similarly, **Daulton Varsho** benefits from a high-upside combination of park factors and a favorable matchup against Young, pushing his efficiency score into elite territory for our squad. Meanwhile, **Luis Arraez** (69.53) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (68.02) are core starts; the latter remains particularly valuable today given the synergy between his plate profile and the stolen base opportunities afforded by the opposing battery.\n\nThe decision to bench **Masyn Winn** (42.65) was a tight call, as his ability to steal bases is a stylistic fit for our scarcity-driven strategy. However, the 33% rain risk at his venue, combined with a tough matchup against a sharp arm in Brown, suppressed his score just enough to keep him on the pine in favor of the higher raw efficiency of **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Bryson Stott**. We are monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Geraldo Perdomo**, but assuming he holds that #3 spot, his projected volume remains superior to the bench alternatives. We continue to hold **Jonathan Aranda** in reserve as his sub-40 score reflects a negative platoon edge against Detmers, underscoring our commitment to efficiency over sentimentality. Finally, we remain mindful of the risks posed to **Will Smith** and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, both of whom are facing elite or near-elite arms; they remain in the lineup for their floor, but their production will be closely monitored against their respective pitchers' xERA metrics.",
